{
  "reason": "Pins screenshot delivery and generic image viewing through declared sources; local reads use the owning conversation, and adding an image targets the current composer without sending. Image paths are normalized before serving; exact producer-provided embeds prevent reconstructed filenames, and missing images remain inspectable with explicit retry. Sent attachment previews inherit their transcript owner when optimistic snapshots omit it, so original-file reads retain conversation scope. Nonvisual models omit image bytes only from their requests; saved image content still renders after reload, including image-only turns. Shell captures can lack structured tool media: explicit assistant image embeds publish exact files from the managed output directory before rendering and on history restore, without admitting prose, stdout, arbitrary paths or another conversation's nested directory. Successful file reads and host visual exports preserve exact original paths through live projection and cold history, including the source alias of pooled image bytes; no sibling worktree or export directory is authorized.",
